 Backport of upstream fix 1c8234eb20bc8afd396b89999a00f06b61d72d7b
 (backport: [i18n] Routing fix #70761 (#70976)).
 .
 Next.js allowed the internal locale query params (__nextLocale,
 __nextDefaultLocale, __nextInferredLocaleFromDefault) to be smuggled in via the
 request URL. When i18n is not configured, or when the supplied locale values are
 not valid configured locales, a spoofed __nextLocale produces an invalid routing
 condition that lets pathname-based middleware authorization be bypassed. These
 params must be stripped before routing/authorization decisions are made.
